CONCLUSION: T=1 is exactly standard KD. Unscaled KL -> 0 as T -> inf,
but the T^2-scaled term used in the loss converges to a nonzero
logit-matching constant (0.1085 here), NOT to 0. The abstract's
'T -> inf reverts to SFT' holds for the unscaled KL term; with the
T^2 factor the limit is logit matching. Colab driver therefore
treats T as trust-in-teacher (small T = strong KD, large T = weak
regularisation toward the frozen base) and reports per-arm results
rather than assuming the T -> inf limit equals plain SFT.
